        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=4$. Intercepts: $(0,0)$ and $(\\tfrac12,0)$. Vertex: $(\\tfrac14,-\\tfrac14)$. Opens upwards; axis $x=\\tfrac14$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-2)^2-4(4)(0)\\\\\\Delta&=4\\\\4x^2-2x&=0\\\\2x(2x-1)&=0\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }\\tfrac12.\\end{align*}$$\nThere are two distinct real $x$-intercepts. The $y$-intercept is $(0,0)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x_{\\mathrm v}&=\\frac{0+\\tfrac12}{2}=\\tfrac14\\\\y_{\\mathrm v}&=4(\\tfrac14)^2-2(\\tfrac14)\\\\y_{\\mathrm v}&=-\\tfrac14.\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola opens upwards, with axis $x=\\tfrac14$.",
