        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=8$. $x$-intercepts: $(-2-\\sqrt2,0)$ and $(-2+\\sqrt2,0)$. $y$-intercept: $(0,2)$. Vertex: $(-2,-2)$. Opens upwards; axis $x=-2$.\n\nUse the quadratic formula for the irrational intercepts.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=4^2-4(1)(2)\\\\\\Delta&=8\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt8}{2}\\\\x&=-2\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\x_{\\mathrm v}&=-\\frac4{2(1)}=-2\\\\y_{\\mathrm v}&=(-2)^2+4(-2)+2\\\\y_{\\mathrm v}&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\Delta>0$, there are two distinct real $x$-intercepts. The $y$-intercept is $(0,2)$. The parabola opens upwards and has axis $x=-2$.",
